                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71ae1d0f-6ad1-3524-a6c8-0901fe7f4cd4",
                        "entry_id": "e1c5d19f-74da-32a6-8b1c-452b209788b8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "экон. денежный сбор, взимаемый соответствующими государственными органами при выполнении ими определённых функций"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "61037396-ded5-457b-93ca-4ad89fa021ce",
                                "sense_id": "71ae1d0f-6ad1-3524-a6c8-0901fe7f4cd4",
                                "text": "Правительство России решило ввести ввозную пошлину на игровые приставки."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73348960-537b-30ae-8550-5a2867f3748d",
                        "entry_id": "e1c5d19f-74da-32a6-8b1c-452b209788b8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. перен. то же, что сбор"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ded7ff20-94f7-47c7-8f45-4748d8210caf",
                                "sense_id": "73348960-537b-30ae-8550-5a2867f3748d",
                                "text": "Брали дани и пошлины // За все годы прошлые."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c821fb05-1a97-43b9-8528-d6ef259e3149",
                        "source_entry_id": "e1c5d19f-74da-32a6-8b1c-452b209788b8",
                        "source_sense_description": "денежный сбор, взимаемый соответствующими государственными органами",
                        "target_lang_word": "duty",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "duty",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65413b6f-b72e-38ac-9943-1ec57741c4c6",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which one is morally or legally obligated to do."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57dbe890-0af5-4d5e-bef6-83a0845d4d88",
                                                "sense_id": "65413b6f-b72e-38ac-9943-1ec57741c4c6",
                                                "text": "Do your duty by me! -No, we don't have a duty to keep you abreast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "582db82c-5e4a-4d27-a81f-3b44fbf49216",
                                                "sense_id": "65413b6f-b72e-38ac-9943-1ec57741c4c6",
                                                "text": "1805, 21 October, Horatio Nelson\nEngland expects that every man will do his duty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41c9aa62-7b55-4cb2-97e9-f2a732410b1a",
                                                "sense_id": "65413b6f-b72e-38ac-9943-1ec57741c4c6",
                                                "text": "Captain Edward Carlisle[…]felt a curious sensation of helplessness seize upon him as he met her steady gaze,[…]; he could not tell what this prisoner might do. He cursed the fate which had assigned such a duty, cursed especially that fate which forced a gallant soldier to meet so superb a woman as this under handicap so hard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e523b5c-e048-4dde-9348-1b2e7e8927a5",
                                                "sense_id": "65413b6f-b72e-38ac-9943-1ec57741c4c6",
                                                "text": "Charles had not been employed above six months at Darracott Place, but he was not such a whopstraw as to make the least noise in the performance of his duties when his lordship was out of humour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f5f2adb-584c-429d-bbd0-b1c121686fc1",
                                                "sense_id": "65413b6f-b72e-38ac-9943-1ec57741c4c6",
                                                "text": "British journalists shun complete respectability, feeling a duty to be ready to savage the mighty, or rummage through their bins. Elsewhere in Europe, government contracts and subsidies ensure that press barons will only defy the mighty so far."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "777ae7fc-675e-33e7-b8e8-79e17d7be152",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being at work and responsible for or doing a particular task."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfbbdb16-7b81-47e5-9856-4388e19c5d14",
                                                "sense_id": "777ae7fc-675e-33e7-b8e8-79e17d7be152",
                                                "text": "I’m on duty from 6 pm to 6 am."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "303fa74e-db52-3109-8195-3a98c0b45162",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tax placed on imports or exports; a tariff."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00696a0b-9c3f-4637-a602-f2dd7a5c3d19",
                                                "sense_id": "303fa74e-db52-3109-8195-3a98c0b45162",
                                                "text": "customs duty; excise duty"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7545fa2-9c21-30c5-967b-ae93fc0d134f",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One's due, something one is owed; a debt or fee."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f157c9c-6acb-4457-9bbd-d04e5c925974",
                                                "sense_id": "c7545fa2-9c21-30c5-967b-ae93fc0d134f",
                                                "text": "Take that which is thy duty, and goo thy waye."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1da11481-4e3c-39f9-9133-32759868d47a",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Respect; reverence; regard; act of respect; homage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a32aad5-0c48-4f44-9085-ae92f6eee7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "1da11481-4e3c-39f9-9133-32759868d47a",
                                                "text": "my duty to you"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a0a3ff9-8188-4086-8f54-6ce65b7caf9b",
                                                "sense_id": "1da11481-4e3c-39f9-9133-32759868d47a",
                                                "text": "It [the letter] was written with a plain, unaffected, homely piety that I knew to be genuine, and ended with ‘my duty to my ever darling’—meaning myself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c21fa5f-ca55-3c83-bac1-7f3499a63ddb",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The efficiency of an engine in work done per unit of fuel; particularly, the number of pounds of water which a steam pumping engine can raise one foot by burning one bushel or hundredweight of coal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e9226f6-4344-36f0-a1cc-3b41f7c06c87",
                                        "entry_id": "a30dd9d8-af9a-32ec-91bb-6eed131ae38e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of urination or defecation, especially for a dog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "euphemistic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7cb43ed-9e82-4499-a7d2-1cd8b7e1f042",
                                                "sense_id": "8e9226f6-4344-36f0-a1cc-3b41f7c06c87",
                                                "text": "The basic idea in housebreaking is not to wait until the puppy sins and then punish him; it is to call nature to your aid and thus make it easy for him to do his duty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "16372126-7fc1-42d0-8b83-f86eac5969c8",
